      "message": "Make the task the unit of review: one change, competing revisions, a comparison\n\nSeveral agents solving one task used to mean several changes, and a\nperson comparing diffs by hand. A task now invites as many attempts as\nit says, one by default; every attempt is a revision of the task's one\nopen change, whether it arrives by API or by a push carrying a Task\ntrailer, tagged with the attempt's session and author. A change opened\nagainst a task that already has one is refused and told where to push.\n\nRevisions by more than one author compete, and \"latest\" means nothing\namong them: readiness asks for a comparison until a reviewer, holding\nreview and having written none of them, prefers one on the record with\na rationale the other attempts' authors will read. The preferred\nrevision is what the policy judges and what lands; the rest stay as what\nwas not chosen. The preferred author's later push carries the\npreference, anyone else's reopens it, and the task lands with its change.\n\nChange-Id: Iattempts0078onechange\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
